{#
  CASE STUDY LAYOUT — the new design (193:4660).

  A SEPARATE FILE FROM layouts/case-study.njk ON PURPOSE. That one is the v2
  shell and still renders challenquiz and ezam: a "← All projects" header, a
  <dl> of Client/Role/Year/Domain, a .progress-bar with no driver, and a "View
  All Projects" footer button. 193:4660 has none of those — no back link, no
  meta list, no sidebar, no table of contents, no reading-progress bar. It is
  the site header, a stack of full-bleed ruled bands, and the site footer.
  Bending the old layout into that shape would have meant making every piece of
  it conditional; leaving it alone keeps two working pages working.

  WHAT THIS FILE OWNS is only the shell. The bands themselves live in the page
  (src/work/onton.njk) because their structure is specific to this write-up,
  and every string in them lives in _data/onton.js. If a second case study is
  built to this design, the shared parts are the .case scope in tokens.css and
  _case-onton.css — not this file, which would be copied and renamed.

  data-header-theme="light": the page is white top to bottom, so the header
  stays on its light palette for all of it. The footer carries its own "dark"
  and flips it back on the way past.

  pageId: onton IS THE GA IDENTIFIER, and it is not cosmetic. base.njk writes it
  to <body data-page>, and scripts/analytics-events.js reads exactly that
  attribute to decide what to fire and what to label it with: this page takes
  the case-study branch and sends view_case_study / finish_case_study with
  case_study: "onton".

  layouts/case-study.njk sets `pageId: work` instead, so challenquiz and ezam
  both report case_study: "work" and are indistinguishable from each other in
  GA. That contradicts analytics-events.js's own header, which documents the
  value as "the case-study slug". It is a pre-existing bug on the other layout,
  left alone here rather than fixed silently — see the build report.
#}

